	(text "POWER IN   -   12 V battery / logger supply, normally 11.5-14.4 V, through three soldered wires. D1 provides reverse-polarity protection. The\nNano VIN branch uses R18; its onboard regulator supplies the hat's 5 V. The TVS and R18 do not guarantee a 21 V surge limit."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 28.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "719fba6c-64ec-45ed-a9d3-b46b02bf87e9")
	)
	(text "SDI-12 DATA   -   R3 limits transmit and fault current; R4 sets the idle\nload. C4 slows transitions and D4 provides ESD protection. Direct 5 V\nGPIO receive thresholds are not guaranteed for every compliant SDI-12\nsender; verify with the intended logger and cable."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 285 32.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "8363d200-3ef6-494a-b803-1c8fdcf08f86")
	)
	(text "ARDUINO NANO R4 ABX00142   -   two Samtec HTSW-115-07-T-S 1x15 strips soldered through BOTH boards; components face inward. Seat header insulators on hat front and use a fixture to hold a 4.00 mm board gap\nduring soldering. Trim solid pin tails to 0.5 mm maximum outside each board. USB-C faces the cable end. Loose pins are not reliable contacts. Program using Arduino Nano R4 in the IDE before potting."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 121.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "3147c2fd-6878-4b80-82bd-93a72880114f")
	)
	(text "HEATER DRIVE + POWER MONITOR   -   heater runs from the battery, never from USB\nalone. Firmware must bound pulse duration to 15 s, monitor V and I, and switch\nOFF on timeout or a fault. Refuse heating above 15 V input. R10 holds the gate\nlow when D9 is high impedance; it is not a watchdog."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430 20.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "51886a3f-7ab7-4e06-8afa-2d1a14760ecb")
	)
	(text "HEATER RESISTOR CHAIN (top side of the centre prong only)   -   17 x 3.3 ohm 1% 0603 in series, 2.6 mm pitch. EXACT Vishay CRCW06033R30FKEAHP, 0.33 W at 70 C. The return runs on the bottom copper of the prong. Use Panasonic ERJ2GEJ5R1X, 0.1 W; resistor tolerance and local temperature affect\nthe margin. First resistor starts outside the epoxy body. Firmware must detect zero heater current as a fault."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 368.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "d2d4a9ed-4e62-42f6-a585-276170415d9b")
	)
